 built into the book itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-15T08:31:54-08:00","id":1355012,"title":"","content":"So a few possible complications that could arise:<br /> <br /> - Does the grimmoire have a guardian bound to it ? If so, breaking it could release it.<br /> <br /> - Does it contain an alarm ? It could warn the maker (like a Banisher or Logophage looking for kindred spirits), any number of guardians, descendants of the creator, etc.<br /> <br /> - What is it made of ? Perfected materials are tough, for example, Orichalcum is chemically inert and indestructible by non-magical means. So mixing that with Wards &amp; Signs makes for a very durable grimmoire.<br /> <br /> - Are there any temper proof measures ? Like hung spells hidden by cloak nimbus to unleash all sorts of contingencies, from damage, to spiriting or teleporting the grimmoire to someone who wants to use it (Fate &amp; Space), changing it into an animal, etc<br /> <br /> - Will the knowledge try to propagate ? For example, the Unforgotten Scion like making grimmoires that have infectious ideas. Or it could trigger a One Ring kind of obsession when they attempt to destroy it.<br /> <br /> - Is the grimmoire the real danger ? What if a pocket sanctum was hidden inside it ? Or an artifact ? Or some kind of key with instructions ?<br /> <br /> - Did they check for the existence of backup copies ? Maybe destroying 